vent counts, overall summary) rather than the timestamps of individual interactions needed to verify increasing times within 600 units. Evidence: there is no direct 1885\u21921460 edge in the full record (step_01); we have neighbors and event counts for the nodes (steps_03, 04) and the overall temporal span of the dataset (step_07) but no per-event timestamps to establish a temporally ordered chain inside the interval. A static 2-hop path 1885\u2192886\u21921460 does exist in the full data (steps_08 and 09), which is a plausible confounder (static connectivity) but without timestamped events we cannot determine whether those interactions occurred in the required temporal order and within 600 time units. Therefore the temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude presence or absence of a genuine cascade.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 47748, "total_output_tokens": 4623, "total_tokens": 52371, "total_latency_ms": 59704, "llm_calls": 11, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}